# Wave W17-S (Route 128 Trench): breath wall — breathing cavern rock: a dark blue-grey trench rock whose seams breathe — warm ember lines standing in its joints and two niche-glows burning low on its face, the Sunken Cavern\u2019s register carried along every wall its road passes (design: the cavern\u2019s drowned mouth in the trench wall, water inside it warmer; the wall kind carries the breathing register, art layer only — the shipped mouth cells themselves stand on cavefloor, byte-preserved). Route 128 Trench\u2019s own wall — the fleet\u2019s only ember-seamed wall: split from Route 127 Trench\u2019s green forest-edge rock by temperature entire, and from Route 126 Trench\u2019s arch-banded door wall by the seams (breath vs masonry).
